  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14129144/assets/f7dfad4e44184f68de36d455e99895fce8c879d4b053c06aa5805c423bdb1bfc.png)\n\nThe gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be a contour plot of $f(x,y)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\nObserve that the given field vectors are perpendicular to the level curves in the following picture.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14129144/assets/9f22df07aac0933106381dce4571e674d656428bf7a976e16bed6d46898f814f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14129144/assets/cecc7f28c20523aac9f153022d64da4233ce995e05df3b3e2886b7fb3b20d089.png)",
